  "title": "Protect the Battery",
  "story": "ION: The workshop assembly line is stalled. Repair this object model to restore the next machine.",
  "lesson": "A property lets assignment run validation. Check type before range, and validate before changing the stored value. 0 <= value <= 100 rejects NaN as well.",
  "objective": "Define Battery(percent), exposing a battery_percent property with a setter. Accept finite int/float values from 0 through 100. Reject bool, strings and None with TypeError. Reject out-of-range values, NaN and infinity with ValueError. Rejected assignments must leave the previous charge intact. The constructor uses the same validation.",
  "sample": "b=Battery(20); b.battery_percent=85; b.battery_percent -> 85",
  "starter_code": "class Battery:\n    def __init__(self, percent):\n        self.battery_percent = percent\n\n    @property\n    def battery_percent(self):\n        return self._percent\n\n    @battery_percent.setter\n    def battery_percent(self, value):\n        pass\n",
  "hint": "A property lets assignment run validation. Check type before range, and validate before changing the stored value. 0 <= value <= 100 rejects NaN as well.",
